            <ArticleTitle>Why gauze dressings should not be the first choice to manage most acute surgical cavity wounds.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>237-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute surgical wounds left to heal by secondary intention are often routinely managed with gauze fabric dressings. This paper reviews research that suggests newer, modern dressings are more cost-effective and cause less pain on removal.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
